# Day 26/50 — Threads

A process doesn't always have to do everything through one single path of execution.

It can contain multiple **threads**, which are smaller units of execution within that process.
Threads can work on different tasks while sharing the process's resources.

For example, an application might handle user input while another thread performs background work.

It's interesting how one application can manage multiple activities at once.
Not every task needs to wait for another to finish.

Sometimes, dividing the work makes the entire system more responsive.

**Because working together doesn't always mean doing the same thing**
